{1 = 1-2}
1.	Say to @wPN{Aradŋu}: this is what @wRN{Šulgi}, 
2.	your lord, says: 

{3 = 3-5}
3.	The man to whom I have sent you is not your subordinate -- he will not @varh[t3102.v1]{accept } @vart[t3102.v2,t3102.v1]{@varn{1 ms. has instead:} change } orders from your hand! 
4.	How can you ignore what he himself has done too, 
5.	and that it is indeed so? 

{6 = 6-15}
6.	As I myself ordered, you were to secure the provinces, 
7.	and to correctly guide the people and @varh[t3102.v3]{make them obedient } @vart[t3102.v4,t3102.v3]{@varn{2 mss. have instead:} secure the foundations of the provinces }. When you approach the cities of the provinces, 
8.	inform yourself precisely of their intentions, and inform yourself of the words of their dignitaries. 
9.	Let my roar @varh[t3102.v5]{be emitted over all the lands } @vart[t3102.v6,t3102.v5]{@varn{1 ms. has instead:} fill all the lands } @vart[t3102.v7,t3102.v5]{@varn{1 ms. has instead:} cover all the lands }. Let my powerful arm, 
10.	my heroic arm, fall upon all the lands. Let my storm @varh[t3102.v8]{cover } @vart[t3102.v9,t3102.v8]{@varn{1 ms. has instead:} be released over } the Land. 
11.	Make the …… disappear into the desert, and the robbers into the fields! 
12.	Until you reach @wPN{Apillaša}, 
13.	my 'Sage of the Assembly', 
14.	……! 
15.	Let ……. 

{16 = 16-17}
16.	That was how I had instructed you. 
17.	Why have you not acted as I ordered you? 

{18 = 18-26}
18.	If I do not make my 'Sage of the Assembly' feel just as important as I am, if he does not sit on a throne on a dais, furnished with a high-quality cloth cover (?), if his feet do not rest on a golden footstool, if he is not allowed by his own highest authority both to appoint and then to remove a governor from his function as governor, an official @varh[t3102.v10]{from his charge } @vart[t3102.v11,t3102.v10]{@varn{some mss. have instead:} from his function as official } @vart[t3102.v12,t3102.v10]{@varn{1 ms. has instead:} from an official }, if he does not kill or blind anyone, if he does not elevate his favourite over others -- how else can he secure the provinces? 

{27 = 27-28}
27.	If you truly love me, 
28.	you will not bear him a grudge! 

{29 = 29-30}
29.	You are important, 
30.	@varh[t3102.v13]{but you do not even know your own soldiers } @vart[t3102.v14,t3102.v13]{@varn{1 ms. has instead:} and you even know the soldiers that are at @wPN{Apillaša's} disposal }. Your eyes have learnt something about @varh[t3102.v15]{these men } @vart[t3102.v16,t3102.v15]{@varn{some mss. have instead:} @wPN{Apillaša's} men }, and about @varh[t3102.v17]{@wPN{Apillaša's} heroism } @vart[t3102.v18,t3102.v17]{@varn{some mss. have instead:} my heroism }. 

{31 = 31-35}
31.	If @varh[t3102.v19]{you, @wPN{Aradŋu}, are indeed my servant } @vart[t3102.v20,t3102.v19]{@varn{some mss. have instead:} you, @wPN{Aradŋu} and @wPN{Apillaša}, are indeed my servants }, you should both pay attention (?) to my written communications. 
